From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:32:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/37] [Seq] RegOfVecToMem: refuse register arrays with reset
 or preset

FirMem carries no reset, so inferring a memory from a register array
that has one silently DROPS the reset: after a reset RE-assertion the
RTL reads 0 while the netlist reads stale data. SAT-provable mismatch
(write -> reset -> read) on the fifo_v3-family mem_q arrays; invisible
to shallow miters. Arrays without reset/preset still infer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/Dialect/Seq/Transforms/RegOfVecToMem.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/Dialect/Seq/Transforms/RegOfVecToMem.cpp b/lib/Dialect/Seq/Transforms/RegOfVecToMem.cpp
index b7c231e58..0d0e9f489 100644
--- a/lib/Dialect/Seq/Transforms/RegOfVecToMem.cpp
+++ b/lib/Dialect/Seq/Transforms/RegOfVecToMem.cpp
@@ -89,6 +89,17 @@ bool RegOfVecToMemPass::analyzeMemoryPattern(FirRegOp reg,
   if (!isArrayType(reg.getType()))
     return false;
 
+  // A register with a reset (or a power-on preset) must NOT become a
+  // seq.firmem: FirMem carries no reset, so the conversion would silently
+  // DROP the array's reset semantics. Concretely: an async-reset register
+  // file reads all-zero after a reset re-assertion in RTL, but the
+  // inferred memory would return whatever was last written -- a real,
+  // SAT-provable mismatch (found via CVA6's fifo_v3 mem_q, which resets
+  // to '0). Leave such arrays as registers; downstream register lowering
+  // handles them correctly.
+  if (reg.getReset() || reg.getPresetAttr())
+    return false;
+
   ArrayGetOp readAccess;
   ArrayInjectOp writeAccess;
   comb::MuxOp writeMux;
